<title>HONG KONG: One dead, 32 injured in Hong Kong parade accident.</title>
<headline>One dead, 32 injured in Hong Kong parade accident.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>A British female tourist was killed and 32 people were injured when a float tipped over at a Hong Kong parade to celebrate the first day of the Lunar New Year, government radio said on Friday.</p>
<p>Three police were injured, one of them seriously.</p>
<p>The accident occurred in Hong Kong's Tsim Sha Tsui tourist district.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6441</p>
